{"page_content": "5.1\nExperiment Requirements\nFLEX-2\nSRD Rev. 1\nsu\ufb03cient size as to allow consistent droplet deployment and positioning for the full range\nof initial droplet diameters, Do , speci\ufb01ed for these tests.\nPosition of pinning beads:\nThe binary array tests shall require a pinning bead spacing\nof L = 12 mm, which will allow for up to three beads to be captured in the 30 mm\nback-lit FOV. This e\ufb00ectively allows two values for spacing lengths between beads (i.e.,\nL = 12 mm and L = 24 mm) and, considering the range of initial droplet diameters (i.e.,\n1.5 mm \u2264Do \u22645.0 mm), will allow for several experimental values for L/Do. Considering\nthis, it is important that the beads either (i) be able tolerate \ufb02ame conditions without\noxidizing and/or degrading or (ii) that they be placed at di\ufb00erent locations on the \ufb01ber in\nsuch a manner that the beads spaced at L = 12 mm are not impacted by tests performed\nwith beads spaced at L = 24 mm.\nDroplet ignition:\nIgnition shall occur by hot-wire ignition.\nIgnitor positioning:\nThe ignitor tip shall be positioned within 1.0 D0 \u22125.0 D0 away\nfrom the anticipated droplet surface. The position of ignitor tip shall be controllable by\ncommand to within 0.5 mm. The ignitor tip shall be removed from viewing area upon\nignition. For the droplet array experiments the ignitor shall be capable of igniting two\ndroplets simultaneously and for the convective \ufb02ow experiments the ignitor shall be capable\nof igniting the droplet at the edge of the smaller of the two HiBM\u2019s FOV, as set for that\nparticular suite of tests.\nIgnitor operation:\nThe time of ignitor power-up and duration of ignitor operation shall be\ncontrollable by command and shall ignite the droplet with the minimum ignition energy\nnecessary to sustain combustion.\nZone of exclusion:\nA spherical zone-of-exclusion of at least 10 D0 extending radially in\nall directions from the droplet center must be maintained free of any objects (where D0\nis the initial droplet diameter) for all tests.\n5.1.3\nInitial Pressure\nThe ambient pressure changes the sooting and radiation characteristics of the droplet.\nAmbient pressure:\nThe initial ambient absolute pressure shall be set to 0.5atm\u22123.0atm\u00b1\n0.05 atm.\nPressure transient::\nThe chamber pressure shall be maintained within \u00b1 10% the initial\nambient pressure throughout each test.\n35", "metadata": {"source": "FLEX-2 SRD Final.pdf", "page": 41}}